From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: UebelAndre <github@uebelandre.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 06:24:10 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(fs): keep directory handles off the resolution path and
 off std::fs::read_dir on wasm

Under the VS Code WebAssembly runtime, closing some directory handles
fails with EBADF (its virtual root among them), and the standard
library turns a failing `closedir` into an abort. The workspace walk
reached that root for an external file without a repository marker, and
the whole server went down a second after the first Bazel data arrived.

The resolution path no longer lists directories at all: the workspace
walk and the BUILD file lookup probe the marker files by name, which is
also cheaper. The listings that remain (load path completion) go through
`dir::read_dir`, which on wasm opens the directory with `open`, reads it
with `fd_readdir` and ignores a failing `close`; natively it is the
standard library's listing. `libc` is now a dependency on every target.

The walk also no longer stats the directories it passes. Under Node's
WASI a symbolic link that leaves a preopened directory, which is what
every external repository in Bazel's repo contents cache is, fails to
stat as the last path component while paths through it resolve; the
marker probes only ever go through it, so a file inside such a
repository finds its root again.
